lattice-surgery-teleport demo — NOTICE

This directory (apps/lattice-surgery-teleport/) is a CPU-only stim and
PyMatching simulation of logical teleportation by lattice surgery. It is not
a reproduction of the ETH Zurich superconducting device and it does not
include that device's noise table or gate schedule.

Paper (attribution, figures not copied):
  Luca Hofele, Yongxin Song, Áron Márton, Ian Hesner, Ilya Besedin, Jakob
  Ekert, Jonathan Trebst, François Swiadek, Felix Henrich, Dante Colao Zanuz,
  Mohsen Bahrami Panah, Lukas Bödeker, Nicholas Gialouris, Chrysander D. Hagen,
  Marek Pechal, Jean-Claude Besse, Markus Müller, Christoph Hellings, and
  Andreas Wallraff, "Teleportation of Logical Qubits using Lattice Surgery
  with Superconducting Circuits", arXiv:2611.23165
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.23165
  Preprint date on the arXiv HTML: 17 November 2026.

  Found via a bookmarked X post by @AndreasAtETH. The post was not fetched.
  The URL below was supplied with the task and the scientific claims were
  checked against the arXiv HTML, not against the post:
  https://x.com/AndreasAtETH/status/2123013303689515201

Hardware numbers quoted from the paper (41 qubits, distance 3, gate and
readout errors, memory logical error rates, teleportation success
probabilities 0.57 / 0.65 modular and 0.65 / 0.73 optimized) are marked
QUOTED. They are not outputs of this simulation.

